#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Alabama
#> pause: 45
#> must: Montana
#> must: Alabama
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: 1!G;h;$!d
# 11. Reverse the order of lines, like tac. Pement: sed '1!G;h;$!d'
# Line 1 is held (h). Every later line first appends the hold space to itself
# (G), so the pattern space is "this line, then everything before it in
# reverse", then h saves that. $!d deletes all but the last line, which is
# the whole file upside down. Watch Montana come out first.
# Try: the sheet's second form,  #ARGS -n  with  1!G;h;$p
1!G;h;$!d

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska
Iowa
Kansas
Montana
